.TH IMGX 1 "2026-11-02" "imgx 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imgx \- convert images between common formats from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY imgx
.I input ...
.RI [ options ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imgx
converts image files between formats.
It reads SVG, PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF, TIFF, GIF, BMP, ICO and a few others,
and writes PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF or TIFF.
.PP
Inputs may be files, directories, or glob patterns.
A directory is walked recursively and every file with a recognised image
extension is converted.
.PP
The output format comes from
.BR \-f ,
or is inferred from the extension of
.BR \-o .
It defaults to PNG.
Without
.BR \-o ,
output is written next to each source file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " " \fIpath\fR
Where to write.
A path ending in an image extension names a single output file.
Anything else is treated as a directory, created if it does not exist, and
the input folder structure is mirrored inside it.
.BR \-o " must be a directory when converting more than one file."
If both
.B \-f
and an
.B \-o
file extension are given and they disagree, it is an error rather than a
silently renamed file.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIfmt\fR
One of
.BR png ,
.BR jpeg ,
.BR webp ,
.BR avif ,
.BR tiff .
Default
.BR png .
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIpx\fR
Target width.
SVGs are rasterized at exactly this width, so the result is crisp at any
size.
Raster images are only ever shrunk; a width at or above the source width is
ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-height \fIpx\fR
Target height, preserving aspect ratio.
Ignored when
.B \-\-width
is also given.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-scale " " \fIn\fR
SVG only.
Render at
.I n
times the intrinsic size.
.BR \-s " 2 gives a retina export."
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " " \fI1\-100\fR
Encoder quality for
.BR jpeg ,
.B webp
and
.BR avif .
Ignored for
.B png
and
.BR tiff ,
which are lossless.
Default 85.
Quality 100 is the best a lossy codec offers, not a lossless mode.
.TP
.B \-\-background \fIcss\fR
The colour used to fill transparent pixels when writing JPEG, which has no
alpha channel.
Accepts
.BR #rrggbb ,
.BR #rgb ,
.BR "rgb(r,g,b)"
or one of
.BR white ,
.BR black ,
.BR gray ,
.BR grey ,
.BR red ,
.BR green ,
.BR blue .
Default
.BR white .
An unrecognised colour is an error rather than a silent fallback.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace destination files that already exist.
Without this flag an existing file is skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve inputs, outputs and formats, print what would be written, and exit
without touching the filesystem.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage to standard output and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit 0.
.SH FORMATS
One row per format.
The
.B Read
column lists the formats that can be used as an input.
The
.B Write
column lists the formats that can be used as an output.
.TS
allbox tab(:);
lb lb lb lb.
Format:Extension:Read:Write
svg:.svg:yes:no
png:.png:yes:yes
jpeg:.jpg:yes:yes
webp:.webp:yes:yes
avif:.avif:yes:yes
tiff:.tiff:yes:yes
gif:.gif:yes:no
bmp:.bmp:yes:no
ico:.ico:yes:no
tga:.tga:yes:no
pnm:.pnm:yes:no
heic:.heic:macOS:no
heif:.heif:macOS:no
psd:.psd:macOS:no
pdf:.pdf:macOS:no
camera raw:.dng ...:macOS:no
.TE
.PP
.B svg
is rasterized with resvg, so
.B -w
and
.B -s
produce genuinely sharp vectors at any size.
.PP
The
.B heic ,
.B heif ,
.B psd ,
.B pdf
and camera raw formats are handled through
.BR sips (1)
on macOS and are unavailable elsewhere.
.PP
SVG is not an output format.
Vectorising a photograph does not recover the curves it was drawn from.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file converted, or was skipped because it already existed.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file failed, or the arguments were invalid, or no input was
given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a diagram for a web page, at exactly 2400 pixels wide:
.PP
.RS
.EX
imgx diagram.svg \-w 2400
.EE
.RE
.PP
Produce a format macOS cannot write on its own:
.PP
.RS
.EX
imgx screenshot.png \-f webp \-q 90 \-o images/
.EE
.RE
.PP
Convert a folder tree into a build directory that does not exist yet:
.PP
.RS
.EX
imgx screenshots/ \-f webp \-q 90 \-o build/webp
.EE
.RE
.PP
Write one file to an exact name:
.PP
.RS
.EX
imgx logo.svg \-o static/logo\-2x.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check what a conversion would do before doing it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
imgx "static/**/*.png" \-f avif \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
.SH AUTOMATION
.B imgx
never prompts, never opens a pager, and never requires a terminal, so it can
be driven from a script or an agent without a pseudo-terminal.
.PP
Progress goes to standard output, one line per file, in a fixed shape:
.PP
.RS
.EX
\fIstatus\fP  \fIsource\fP \-> \fIdestination\fP  \fIW\fPx\fIH\fP  \fIsize\fP
.EE
.RE
.PP
.I status
is one of
.BR ok ,
.BR skip ,
.B plan
or
.BR fail .
It is left-padded to four characters, so the columns line up; split on
whitespace rather than on fixed offsets.
.B ok
lines end with dimensions and a byte size;
.B skip
and
.B plan
lines do not.
.B fail
lines go to standard error and carry the reason.
The last line is a summary such as "3 converted, 1 skipped".
With
.BR \-\-dry\-run
the summary instead reads "N file(s) would be written".
.PP
Runs are idempotent.
An existing destination is skipped rather than overwritten, so re-running a
command after a partial failure only redoes the work that did not finish.
Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to resolve inputs and destinations without writing anything.
.PP
Because skip lines are not failures, an agent that wants a hard assertion
should check the exit status and the failure count in the summary rather than
assuming an empty output means nothing happened.
.SH LIMITATIONS
.TP
.B No upscaling
Raster images are never enlarged by
.BR \-\-width .
Passing a width larger than the source leaves the file unchanged, by design.
.TP
.B Animation
Animated GIF and WebP use the first frame only.
.TP
.B Colour profiles
ICC profiles are not carried into the output.
Pixels are not converted, so an image tagged Display P3 or AdobeRGB is
written with the same numbers but without its tag, and viewers will read
them as sRGB.
Convert to sRGB before using
.B imgx
if colour accuracy matters.
.TP
.B EXIF orientation
The rotation flag in EXIF is not applied.
Photographs whose pixels are stored sideways will be written sideways.
.TP
.B Metadata
EXIF, XMP and GPS data are not preserved.
.TP
.B Decoder safety
.B imgx
has no sandbox.
Malformed or hostile images are decoded by the same native libraries a
browser uses, running as your user, so treat an image from an untrusted
source with the caution you would apply to opening it in a browser.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B completions/_imgx
zsh completion function, shipped in the imgx source tree.
Copy or symlink it into any directory on
.BR $fpath .
oh-my-zsh users can use
.BR ~/.oh-my-zsh/custom/completions ,
which is already on
.BR $fpath .
Then open a new shell, since completion functions are indexed at startup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sips (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR exiftool (1)
